1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:12,092
In the late nineteenth century, one question had painters, scientists, and horse breeders arguing. When a horse gallops, do all four hooves leave the ground at the same time?

2
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:17,204
The human eye couldn't see it. Painters drew it each in their own way.

3
00:00:17,404 --> 00:00:23,522
To settle the doubt, a photographer lined up twelve cameras with threads that the horse snapped as it ran past.

4
00:00:24,222 --> 00:00:28,330
The answer was yes. And without meaning to, he opened the door to cinema.

5
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:35,990
This is the story of cinema. How still photos learned to move, to speak, and to burst with color.
